WEBVTT

00:00:09.780 --> 00:00:14.030
Um... Vanitas?

00:00:14.030 --> 00:00:18.580
Wouldn't it be better to lie down?

00:00:18.580 --> 00:00:22.830
We only have one blanket, so...

00:00:22.830 --> 00:00:25.500
I'll join you.

00:00:30.090 --> 00:00:31.420
No.

00:00:31.420 --> 00:00:35.050
Truth be told, I'm at my limit
in so many ways.

00:00:35.050 --> 00:00:36.680
Really?

00:02:02.100 --> 00:02:07.270
"The Case Study of Vanitas"

00:02:22.240 --> 00:02:23.830
Vanitas!

00:02:26.330 --> 00:02:28.500
Jeanne.

00:02:32.500 --> 00:02:34.800
That wound...

00:02:36.130 --> 00:02:38.510
You were poisoned?

00:02:38.510 --> 00:02:40.430
I must suck it out of you at once!

00:02:40.430 --> 00:02:42.680
It's already been dealt with.

00:02:42.680 --> 00:02:44.140
Yes, but...!

00:02:45.890 --> 00:02:47.810
Don't touch me.

00:02:47.810 --> 00:02:51.520
You've come for the Beast, haven't you?

00:02:51.520 --> 00:02:54.980
So go. Pay me no mind.

00:02:57.440 --> 00:03:00.700
How could I possibly leave you like this?

00:03:10.040 --> 00:03:12.790
It should be up ahead.

00:03:21.130 --> 00:03:24.510
One moment while I light a fire.

00:03:24.510 --> 00:03:28.020
Damn it all. This couldn't get any worse.

00:03:28.020 --> 00:03:32.230
That infernal brat. I will slaughter
him the next time we meet.

00:03:32.230 --> 00:03:33.940
Damn him.

00:03:42.780 --> 00:03:46.740
Good. This will provide some warmth.

00:03:46.740 --> 00:03:48.870
Now, Vanitas!

00:03:50.450 --> 00:03:51.960
Disrobe!

00:03:51.960 --> 00:03:53.460
<i>Quoi?!</i>

00:03:53.460 --> 00:03:55.040
Don't give me that.

00:03:55.040 --> 00:03:58.460
Your clothes are damp from the snow.

00:03:58.460 --> 00:04:00.460
You'll never warm up like that.

00:04:00.460 --> 00:04:02.800
You're asking me to strip naked? Here?

00:04:02.800 --> 00:04:05.180
That's right. You don't
mind if I help, do you?

00:04:05.180 --> 00:04:06.470
No! Wait!

00:04:06.470 --> 00:04:07.810
I see!

00:04:07.810 --> 00:04:12.560
You wish to warm me with
your bare body next to mine!

00:04:12.560 --> 00:04:15.150
What's gotten into you?
You're quite forward today.

00:04:15.150 --> 00:04:16.480
That's right!

00:04:16.480 --> 00:04:18.110
<i>Quoi?!</i>

00:04:20.900 --> 00:04:23.400
Dial it down, Jeanne! This isn't like you!

00:04:23.400 --> 00:04:24.860
Have a little modesty!

00:04:24.860 --> 00:04:26.280
Quit your yapping!

00:04:26.280 --> 00:04:28.200
Lives are on the line!

00:04:28.200 --> 00:04:30.490
Now let me remove your clothes!

00:04:34.750 --> 00:04:37.290
Yes, ma'am.

00:04:37.290 --> 00:04:39.420
Huh? Vanitas?!

00:04:51.430 --> 00:04:54.640
He has scars all over his body.

00:04:57.560 --> 00:04:59.020
Don't.

00:05:00.190 --> 00:05:03.780
Leave that glove on.

00:05:03.780 --> 00:05:05.570
As you wish.

00:05:25.170 --> 00:05:28.050
Forgive me, Vanitas.

00:05:28.050 --> 00:05:30.930
It's my fault

00:05:30.930 --> 00:05:33.220
this happened to you.

00:05:37.770 --> 00:05:40.940
Are you referring to this wound?

00:05:40.940 --> 00:05:45.110
Or do you mean your battle with the Beast?

00:05:45.110 --> 00:05:46.950
Both.

00:05:47.950 --> 00:05:50.450
Who is Chloé?

00:05:51.410 --> 00:05:56.870
Do you know who the Beast really is?

00:06:04.050 --> 00:06:09.390
My parents were Lord Ruthven's students.

00:06:09.390 --> 00:06:15.640
When I was little, we would all
travel together to all sorts of places.

00:06:15.640 --> 00:06:20.480
Once, I was left in the
care of Marquis d'Apchier

00:06:20.480 --> 00:06:23.940
at his castle in Gévaudan.

00:06:26.490 --> 00:06:29.530
Pleased to meet you, Jeanne. I am--

00:06:29.530 --> 00:06:32.120
It's a talking doll!

00:06:42.500 --> 00:06:47.760
There dwells the vampire
hidden away by Marquis d'Apchier,

00:06:47.760 --> 00:06:49.590
Chloé d'Apchier.

00:06:49.590 --> 00:06:56.310
A vampire whose existence was hidden,
yet continued to live among humankind.

00:06:57.350 --> 00:07:00.100
She looked like a young girl,

00:07:00.100 --> 00:07:05.110
but Chloé was a vampire who had
lived even longer than Lord Ruthven.

00:07:05.110 --> 00:07:11.200
She taught me many things,
including lessons and games.

00:07:11.200 --> 00:07:14.280
It was as if I had a big sister.
I was so happy.

00:07:14.280 --> 00:07:19.120
Each day was truly a joy.

00:07:19.120 --> 00:07:23.250
I don't wanna go home yet.

00:07:28.800 --> 00:07:31.800
Come visit me in Gévaudan again.

00:07:31.800 --> 00:07:36.220
I'll look forward to the day
when I can see how you've grown.

00:07:42.390 --> 00:07:46.150
But when we did meet once more,

00:07:46.150 --> 00:07:48.110
I was a bourreau sent to slay her,

00:07:48.110 --> 00:07:52.450
for she was now the
one known as the Beast.

00:07:52.450 --> 00:07:54.320
Bourreaus are but tools.

00:07:54.320 --> 00:07:57.830
We need only follow orders.

00:07:57.830 --> 00:07:59.540
"I don't understand."

00:07:59.540 --> 00:08:01.750
"Why you?" I thought.

00:08:01.750 --> 00:08:05.880
But I was not supposed
to harbor such doubts.

00:08:05.880 --> 00:08:08.550
So I hesitated.

00:08:08.550 --> 00:08:12.550
I was unable to slay her.

00:08:12.550 --> 00:08:14.390
And so...

00:08:14.390 --> 00:08:17.760
I beg you. Allow me to go
once more, Lord Ruthven.

00:08:17.760 --> 00:08:20.930
If the Beast that has
appeared truly is Chloé,

00:08:20.930 --> 00:08:23.190
it is my responsibility.

00:08:25.810 --> 00:08:30.190
I will not make the same mistake again.

00:08:30.190 --> 00:08:34.200
I <i>will</i> slay the Beast this time.

00:08:35.660 --> 00:08:38.450
So, that's why you're here?

00:08:38.450 --> 00:08:40.040
Truly?

00:08:44.960 --> 00:08:46.460
Vanitas?

00:08:46.460 --> 00:08:53.340
It's not as if you bear any
hatred toward her, do you?

00:08:53.340 --> 00:08:54.970
You're feverish!

00:08:56.050 --> 00:08:58.050
I'll fetch some water.

00:08:58.050 --> 00:08:59.760
Yes.

00:08:59.760 --> 00:09:03.560
It wasn't hatred.

00:09:03.560 --> 00:09:06.190
It wasn't.

00:09:06.190 --> 00:09:07.980
I...

00:09:09.060 --> 00:09:10.150
Vanitas.

00:09:10.150 --> 00:09:11.690
Lou...

00:09:17.030 --> 00:09:18.370
Lou?

00:09:18.370 --> 00:09:22.370
What does he mean? Is that someone's name?

00:09:24.660 --> 00:09:27.580
Vanitas, you need to drink.

00:09:27.580 --> 00:09:30.290
You'll get dehydrated if you don't.

00:09:30.290 --> 00:09:31.800
Are you sure about this?

00:09:31.800 --> 00:09:36.970
You want to slay the Beast,
and I want to save it.

00:09:36.970 --> 00:09:42.850
We're at cross-purposes,
and that makes us foes.

00:09:42.850 --> 00:09:47.690
Killing me right here may
be in your best interest.

00:09:47.690 --> 00:09:52.520
How could I possibly do that after
you nearly died defending me?!

00:09:52.520 --> 00:09:55.740
You're so naive. You truly are.

00:09:55.740 --> 00:09:59.870
That is why you two,
both you and Noé are...

00:10:05.580 --> 00:10:07.210
Enough.

00:10:07.210 --> 00:10:12.420
If you want me to kill you so badly,
focus on resting while you can.

00:10:15.170 --> 00:10:16.630
Jeanne--

00:10:36.690 --> 00:10:38.320
Hmm?

00:10:38.320 --> 00:10:40.030
It's morning.

00:10:43.990 --> 00:10:45.290
Vanitas?!

00:10:47.620 --> 00:10:50.500
Whatever shall we do if something
has happened to Dante?!

00:10:50.500 --> 00:10:51.380
Calm yourself.

00:10:51.380 --> 00:10:53.540
How, pray tell?!

00:10:58.470 --> 00:11:02.090
I've seen him before. He was with Vanitas.

00:11:05.310 --> 00:11:07.680
Vanitas.

00:11:07.680 --> 00:11:10.140
You're well enough to be up and about.

00:11:10.140 --> 00:11:12.270
What a relief.

00:11:12.270 --> 00:11:14.150
I'm so relieved you're...

00:11:24.780 --> 00:11:28.790
Come to think of it, even if
I simply wished to warm his body,

00:11:28.790 --> 00:11:32.540
I-I-I was almost entirely
naked right next to him!

00:11:32.540 --> 00:11:34.960
I forced him to disrobe against his will!

00:11:34.960 --> 00:11:38.090
And then I forced him
to drink from my mouth!

00:11:38.090 --> 00:11:40.220
That makes me...

00:11:40.220 --> 00:11:41.760
...a total pervert!

00:11:41.760 --> 00:11:43.550
No! This was different!

00:11:43.550 --> 00:11:46.850
I'm the reason he was poisoned!

00:11:46.850 --> 00:11:49.430
As thanks for saving me...

00:11:49.430 --> 00:11:53.190
No! I cannot <i>ever</i> be in such a man's debt.

00:11:53.190 --> 00:11:56.230
What really happened yesterday
was a bid to save his life,

00:11:56.230 --> 00:11:58.440
and nothing more!

00:11:58.440 --> 00:11:59.990
However...

00:12:02.280 --> 00:12:05.410
Vanitas looked so dismayed.

00:12:05.410 --> 00:12:08.160
I'd never seen him like that.

00:12:08.160 --> 00:12:10.700
Unlike his usual arrogance,

00:12:10.700 --> 00:12:14.830
I found his vulnerability
refreshing for some reason.

00:12:14.830 --> 00:12:16.960
Dare I say it was adorable?

00:12:16.960 --> 00:12:18.420
Silly me!

00:12:19.630 --> 00:12:21.420
What are you thinking?!

00:12:21.420 --> 00:12:23.470
It's the perfect chance, Jeanne!

00:12:23.470 --> 00:12:27.300
Vanitas would never wish to be
seen like that if he could help it!

00:12:27.300 --> 00:12:31.020
That means I now have him at my mercy.

00:12:32.350 --> 00:12:36.060
Now then, today's the day the tide turns.

00:12:36.060 --> 00:12:39.780
I want you to recall how I took
advantage of you last night,

00:12:39.780 --> 00:12:42.440
then see you get your knickers in a knot!

00:12:44.610 --> 00:12:46.160
Good morning, Vanitas!

00:12:46.160 --> 00:12:49.200
Feeling all better now?

00:12:49.200 --> 00:12:52.540
Jeanne, I thought you'd never wake up.

00:12:58.710 --> 00:13:01.760
What's with you?
Got your knickers in a knot?

00:13:01.760 --> 00:13:04.430
He's back to normal? He totally is!

00:13:04.430 --> 00:13:07.090
Maybe even a bit more terse than usual!

00:13:07.090 --> 00:13:11.060
What? Something bad happen to you?

00:13:11.060 --> 00:13:13.680
None of your business.

00:13:13.680 --> 00:13:18.110
You're... human?

00:13:18.110 --> 00:13:20.900
No, a vampire!

00:13:20.900 --> 00:13:23.860
Wrong again. I'm a dham.

00:13:25.780 --> 00:13:30.240
Sorry. I've been out of sorts ever
since I was separated from my partner.

00:13:30.240 --> 00:13:31.540
Johann!

00:13:33.500 --> 00:13:34.870
Dante!

00:13:34.870 --> 00:13:36.830
Thank heavens!

00:13:36.830 --> 00:13:39.590
How would I ever be able to apologize
to Riche if something happened to you?!

00:13:39.590 --> 00:13:42.250
Shut up, already! You're not my keeper!

00:13:42.250 --> 00:13:44.760
Nice work finding us here, baldy.

00:13:44.760 --> 00:13:47.590
I just followed that
wisp of chimney smoke.

00:13:47.590 --> 00:13:49.430
All that's left is Noé.

00:13:49.430 --> 00:13:52.470
Where the devil is that fool?

00:13:52.470 --> 00:13:55.100
He was taken away.

00:13:55.100 --> 00:13:59.270
I believe it was the Silver Witch.

00:13:59.270 --> 00:14:02.230
After <i>The Book of Vanitas</i> went flying...

00:14:15.450 --> 00:14:18.290
I couldn't follow them any farther.

00:14:18.290 --> 00:14:19.750
Sorry.

00:14:19.750 --> 00:14:21.290
I see.

00:14:21.290 --> 00:14:23.920
So they have my book.

00:14:23.920 --> 00:14:26.050
You care more about
a book than your partner?!

00:14:26.050 --> 00:14:30.470
Why should I have
to worry about that fool?

00:14:30.470 --> 00:14:32.760
His sturdiness is his saving grace.

00:14:32.760 --> 00:14:35.430
He won't kick the bucket so easily.

00:14:35.430 --> 00:14:37.430
I hope you're right.

00:14:47.900 --> 00:14:52.030
Captain! Captain Astolfo!

00:14:52.030 --> 00:14:53.330
Marco?

00:14:53.330 --> 00:14:56.620
At last I've found you!
Are you all right?!

00:14:57.790 --> 00:15:02.880
I begged you to refrain
from acting on your own.

00:15:02.880 --> 00:15:04.920
Where are you going?

00:15:04.920 --> 00:15:08.130
Huh?! Are you a complete fool?

00:15:08.130 --> 00:15:13.430
Why do you think I came
to this godforsaken place?

00:15:13.430 --> 00:15:16.060
Now, let's go.

00:15:16.060 --> 00:15:18.680
The witch's castle awaits.

00:15:18.680 --> 00:15:22.350
Well then, I assume we'll go after them?

00:15:22.350 --> 00:15:25.480
Yes. But before that...

00:15:28.190 --> 00:15:33.490
Let's hear everything you've
been hiding from me, Dante.

00:15:33.490 --> 00:15:36.330
I paid for what you claimed
to be <i>all</i> the information

00:15:36.330 --> 00:15:40.460
about the Beast of Gévaudan.

00:15:40.460 --> 00:15:45.420
If there's anything therein
you've kept from me,

00:15:45.420 --> 00:15:48.710
I no longer require your services.

00:15:50.300 --> 00:15:51.590
Out with it.

00:15:51.590 --> 00:15:58.930
Why are you, the vampires,
and the Church really after the Beast?

00:15:58.930 --> 00:16:01.600
What are you talking about?

00:16:01.600 --> 00:16:06.650
The Beast of Gévaudan
is a curse-bearing vampire.

00:16:06.650 --> 00:16:09.780
It's Chloé, and she's slain
a great many people.

00:16:09.780 --> 00:16:15.370
That's why Lord Ruthven
and the Church want her head.

00:16:15.370 --> 00:16:17.910
It's that simple, is it not?

00:16:17.910 --> 00:16:19.540
Dante.

00:16:19.540 --> 00:16:21.330
Our brief acquaintance is over.

00:16:21.330 --> 00:16:23.210
No, wait!

00:16:23.210 --> 00:16:25.170
Hey.

00:16:25.170 --> 00:16:30.340
Lay a finger on any of my family,
and I <i>will</i> kill you.

00:16:30.340 --> 00:16:32.130
Try me.

00:16:32.130 --> 00:16:36.470
There will be two dim-witted
and dead dhams littering the snow.

00:16:39.100 --> 00:16:42.480
Are you deaf?! I said, wait!

00:16:42.480 --> 00:16:43.730
You, too, Johann!

00:16:43.730 --> 00:16:45.520
But...!

00:16:45.520 --> 00:16:49.900
Okay, relax. I'll talk.

00:16:51.190 --> 00:16:52.530
All right.

00:16:52.530 --> 00:16:56.160
Jeanne, do you think the
Silver Witch that Dante mentioned

00:16:56.160 --> 00:16:59.450
is the Chloé you speak of?

00:16:59.450 --> 00:17:02.120
Well, I believe so.

00:17:02.120 --> 00:17:06.080
Then do you know where
they may have taken Noé?

00:17:06.080 --> 00:17:07.840
I'd ask you to show us the way.

00:17:07.840 --> 00:17:09.130
What?!

00:17:09.130 --> 00:17:11.840
We may be at cross-purposes here.

00:17:11.840 --> 00:17:16.140
But surely Dante's story
has pricked up your ears.

00:17:16.140 --> 00:17:17.970
Bourreaus are but tools.

00:17:17.970 --> 00:17:20.760
We need only follow orders.

00:17:20.760 --> 00:17:23.890
I-I...

00:17:23.890 --> 00:17:27.770
Wait. Why does the Hellfire Witch
know where that little brat lives?

00:17:27.770 --> 00:17:29.270
Shut your piehole, baldy.

00:17:29.270 --> 00:17:30.150
What?!

00:17:30.150 --> 00:17:33.400
You can talk on the way.

00:17:33.400 --> 00:17:35.400
Who put a bug up your butt?

00:17:35.400 --> 00:17:37.660
I'm not annoyed with you or anyone else.

00:17:37.660 --> 00:17:39.200
It's simply...

00:17:39.200 --> 00:17:41.740
...time's a-wasting.

00:17:43.000 --> 00:17:45.000
So that's it.

00:17:45.000 --> 00:17:49.210
If he's worried about his partner,
he should just say so.

00:17:49.210 --> 00:17:51.710
He's one twisted jerk.

00:18:05.430 --> 00:18:07.600
Huh?! Who are you?!

00:18:17.070 --> 00:18:20.490
Sucking blood without
consent is against the law!

00:18:21.990 --> 00:18:25.370
Well now, you're finally awake.

00:18:26.410 --> 00:18:28.170
I want more.

00:18:31.670 --> 00:18:34.590
Give me my pillow back!

00:18:34.590 --> 00:18:38.880
Give it back? But it's not even yours.

00:18:38.880 --> 00:18:41.680
That's true, but you know what I meant!

00:18:41.680 --> 00:18:46.600
I need but one more
mouthful of your blood.

00:18:46.600 --> 00:18:48.850
As I said, sucking blood without consent--

00:18:48.850 --> 00:18:51.730
What a noisy child you are.

00:18:51.730 --> 00:18:56.360
I'm so weak I can't move.
Is it all that blood she drank?

00:18:59.700 --> 00:19:03.910
This is bad. No, it's terrifying.

00:19:07.830 --> 00:19:14.290
Chloé, it is wrong to suck the
blood of those who are unwilling.

00:19:14.290 --> 00:19:15.250
Who's he?

00:19:15.250 --> 00:19:17.380
Actually, right now, anyone will do.

00:19:17.380 --> 00:19:18.760
I'm saved!

00:19:18.760 --> 00:19:20.550
What I meant was,

00:19:20.550 --> 00:19:25.060
it is wrong to suck the
blood of any man but me.

00:19:25.060 --> 00:19:26.310
It's <i>very</i> wrong.

00:19:26.310 --> 00:19:30.770
I'm so jealous I wish to strangle
to death the very man I just saved.

00:19:30.770 --> 00:19:32.810
Oh my, you're jealous?

00:19:32.810 --> 00:19:36.610
You say the most
adorable things, Jean-Jacques.

00:19:36.610 --> 00:19:40.820
Well, how was it, Chloé?

00:19:40.820 --> 00:19:45.280
I'm asking whose blood was
more delectable, his or mine?

00:19:45.280 --> 00:19:50.790
Don't be silly. Of course,
yours tastes better.

00:19:50.790 --> 00:19:52.170
Really?

00:19:52.170 --> 00:19:55.840
I see. Then we have no problem here.

00:19:55.840 --> 00:19:58.840
Silly boy.

00:19:58.840 --> 00:19:59.970
Ouch!

00:19:59.970 --> 00:20:01.510
Murr?!

00:20:01.510 --> 00:20:03.510
That cat is yours?

00:20:03.510 --> 00:20:08.560
We found it wandering the mountain,
so we brought him home with you.

00:20:08.560 --> 00:20:11.560
I dried and mended your clothes.

00:20:11.560 --> 00:20:14.310
Come down once you've changed.

00:20:18.650 --> 00:20:20.900
What a fine fellow!

00:20:22.860 --> 00:20:25.620
Chloé and Jean-Jacques.

00:20:26.620 --> 00:20:28.120
Chloé?!

00:20:28.120 --> 00:20:29.370
Chloé!

00:20:29.370 --> 00:20:31.790
That child is the Beast?!

00:20:37.290 --> 00:20:40.920
I hope Vanitas and the others are safe.

00:20:40.920 --> 00:20:45.550
For now, I'll hear what
those two have to say.

00:20:45.550 --> 00:20:48.560
Everything else can wait.

00:21:04.700 --> 00:21:06.410
Pardon me.

00:21:18.710 --> 00:21:20.880
Automatons?

00:21:20.880 --> 00:21:24.260
No, automated instruments?

00:21:24.260 --> 00:21:27.140
Do come in, young man.

00:21:30.890 --> 00:21:33.350
Let me introduce you, Herman.

00:21:33.350 --> 00:21:35.190
The boy's name is Noé.

00:21:35.190 --> 00:21:40.440
We found him collapsed amid the blizzard,
so we brought him home.

00:21:40.440 --> 00:21:44.950
How do you know my name?

00:21:44.950 --> 00:21:48.280
I learned your name... from her.

